# Windows batch files must check out with CRLF endings. cmd.exe mishandles LF-only
# batch files around parenthesised blocks such as `if errorlevel 1 (`, and the symptom
# is not a parse error - run.bat simply exits 1 having printed nothing at all.
#
# core.autocrlf is `input` on this machine, which normalises to LF on commit and does
# not convert back on checkout, so without this a fresh clone gets broken scripts.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts are the mirror image: LF, whatever the platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

*.java text
*.md text
*.css text
*.js text
*.xml text
*.fxml text
*.ps1 text
